## Why This Is Asked

This tests practical understanding of lock-free IPC, memory ordering, and backpressure under contention.

## Key Concepts

- Lock-free ring buffer across producers and a consumer
- CAS-based enqueue and acquire/release semantics
- Backpressure strategies and fairness
- Testing under contention

## Code Example

```c
// Producer sketch
bool enqueue(ring_t *r, void *d){
  unsigned int pos = atomic_fetch_add(&r->tail, 1, memory_order_relaxed);
  if (pos - r->head >= r->size) return false;
  r->slots[pos % r->size] = d;
  atomic_thread_fence(memory_order_release);
  return true;
}
```

```c
// Consumer sketch
void *dequeue(ring_t *r){
  unsigned int h = atomic_load(&r->head, memory_order_acquire);
  unsigned int t = atomic_load(&r->tail, memory_order_acquire);
  if (h == t) return NULL;
  void *d = r->slots[h % r->size];
  atomic_store(&r->head, h+1);
  return d;
}
```

